cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AttemptDB: a temporal and causal database of coding-agent work"
message: "If you use AttemptDB in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "AttemptDB contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nullarch/attemptdb"
url: "https://github.com/nullarch/attemptdb"
abstract: >-
  AttemptDB is a local-first database of what AI coding agents attempted.
  It captures provider hook events from Claude Code, Codex, Cursor and
  Gemini CLI into an owned storage engine (write-ahead log, Arrow IPC
  segments, atomic manifest generations), separates immutable observed
  facts from inference carrying evidence identifiers and confidence, and
  exposes both SQL and a small question language, AttemptQL, over the
  result.
keywords:
  - coding agents
  - developer observability
  - temporal database
  - provenance
  - local-first software
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
